/-!
# The hyperplane sequence on projective space

For the hyperplane `ι : ℙ(n; R) ⟶ ℙ(n + 1; R)`, `{Xₙ₊₁ = 0}`, and `m : ℤ`, the sequence of sheaves
of modules on `ℙ(n + 1; R)`

  `0 ⟶ O(m) --Xₙ₊₁--> O(m + 1) ⟶ ι_* O(m + 1) ⟶ 0`

is exact. The map `O(m) ⟶ ι_* O(m)` is `ι^♯` on the charts (`hyperplaneRestrict`): the standard
cocycle `Xⱼ / Xᵢ` of `ℙ(n + 1; R)` pulls back to that of `ℙ(n; R)`. Exactness is checked on
small opens (`Scheme.Modules.shortExact_of_locally_exact`): on a basic open `W` of the chart
`Uⱼ`, `j ≤ n`, the sequence of sections is `A --y--> A ⟶ A / (y) ⟶ 0` with `y = Xₙ₊₁ / Xⱼ`
(`hyperplane_app_basicOpen_eq_zero`), and on opens inside `Uₙ₊₁` multiplication by `Xₙ₊₁` is
bijective while `ι_* O(m + 1)` has no nonzero sections.

## Main definitions and results

- `ProjectiveSpace.hyperplaneRestrict n R m : O(m) ⟶ ι_* O(m)`.
- `ProjectiveSpace.mulX_comp_hyperplaneRestrict`: `Xₙ₊₁` vanishes on the hyperplane.
- `ProjectiveSpace.hyperplaneSequence n R m`: the short complex
  `O(m) --Xₙ₊₁--> O(m + 1) ⟶ ι_* O(m + 1)`, and `ProjectiveSpace.hyperplaneSequence_shortExact`.
-/


